  1:Name            D4-SCPYD Copy buffer control logic and DMA low address logic;
  2:PartNo          108395-OO1;
  3:Revision        01;
  4:Date            16/5/26;
  5:Designer        Dave Henry;
  6:Company         Breadboarding Labs;
  7:Location        None;
  8:Assembly        None;
  9:Device          g16v8;
 10:
 11:/* 16/05/2026 V1 Initial version converted from PALASM format in COMPAQ design doc         */
 12:/*                                                                                         */
 13:/*******************************************************************************************/
 14:/*                                                                                         */
 15:/*******************************************************************************************/
 16:/*
 17:DESCRIPTION
 18:This PAL implements the logic to enable the copy buffer (high to low halves 
 19:of the 16 bit bus). It also drives the A0 and BHE lines as appropriate during
 20:DMA.
 21:Rev A changes the COPYHL enable during byte DMA operations to the high half of 
 22:the bus. The timing is made earlier by changing to IORC from MWTC. 
 23:Rev D changes the polarity of the AEN2 signal for logic reduction on the D3PE 
 24:D4-PROCESSOR board (with 80387).
 25:
 26:Note that changes were required to LM16 to avoid Unstable Output errors in the simulation
 27:!LM16 changed to registered with BALE as the clock and Pin 11 defined as oe output enable active high
 28:!HLDA moved to pin 19
 29:*/
 30:
 31:/* Pin Map 
 32:                               ______________
 33:                              |   D4-SCPYD   |
 34:                     BALE x---|1           20|---x Vcc                      
 35:                    !IO16 x---|2           19|---x !HLDA                    
 36:                    !MWTC x---|3           18|---x !LM16                    
 37:                    !MRDC x---|4           17|---x XA0                      
 38:                    !IOWX x---|5           16|---x !BHE                     
 39:                    !IORC x---|6           15|---x !DAEN                    
 40:                   !DAEN1 x---|7           14|---x !COPYHL                  
 41:                     AEN2 x---|8           13|---x !COPYEN                  
 42:                     !M16 x---|9           12|---x !DAEN2                   
 43:                      GND x---|10          11|---x !oe                       
 44:                              |______________|
 45:*/
 46:
 47:
 48:/* PIN 1 = !M16 ; */
 49:PIN 1 = BALE ;
 50:PIN 2 = !IO16 ;
 51:PIN 3 = !MWTC ;
 52:PIN 4 = !MRDC ;
 53:PIN 5 = !IOWX ;

